# PhysioJEPA progress

Last updated: 2026-08-05

## 1. Changes made

- Added root-level `MODEL_TEST_METRICS.md`, comparing completed test metrics
  and independently selected validation AUROC/AP across the tracked model
  families.
- Recorded completed full-test results for FCN and supervised PatchTST in the
  root comparison and the detailed baseline Markdown reports.
- Added `jobs/jepa/resume_checkpoints.py` support for Lightning emergency
  checkpoints named `hpc_ckpt_*.ckpt`, so wall-time signal checkpoints are
  discoverable on restart.
- Kept native JEPA resume enabled with 30-minute rolling checkpoints and
  configuration-fingerprint validation.
- Updated the two-GPU JEPA launch scripts to use `torchrun --standalone
  --nproc_per_node=2` from a normal `sbatch` task (no `srun`).
- Added node exclusions for the two nodes where two-GPU rank 1 failed during
  CUDA setup.
- Added `jobs/jepa/train_patch_jepa_1gpu_debug.sbatch`, which overrides the
  training config to one GPU and uses a separate checkpoint directory.
- Added this progress document. No commits or remote changes were made.

## 2. Working

- One-GPU JEPA training starts successfully on `a100_short` and sees
  `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES: [0]`.
- Current job `26107011` is running on `a100-4013`. Last observed progress was
  epoch 0, batch 401/2125 (~19%), at about 0.29 batches/sec.
- The one-GPU run uses the complete indexed leakage-safe dataset: 272,068
  training samples and 14,540 validation samples, with no sample limits.
- The one-GPU trainer logs `SLURM auto-requeueing enabled` when submitted with
  `--requeue --signal=B:SIGUSR1@180`.
- Supervised baseline jobs remain active and are writing checkpoints/logs.
- FCN full evaluation job `26027817` completed successfully and produced its
  paper-style metrics JSON and prediction artifact.
- Full supervised PatchTST evaluation completed and produced its prediction
  artifact; its best logged validation AUROC/AP were 0.881/0.285.
- FCN's best logged validation AUROC/AP were 0.869/0.345, selected
  independently rather than from one jointly optimized checkpoint.
- Completed FCN test metrics: AUROC 0.7903, average precision 0.1911,
  accuracy 0.4523, F1 0.1242, recall 0.9037, specificity 0.4320.
- Completed supervised PatchTST test metrics: AUROC 0.8688, average
  precision 0.2766, accuracy 0.6702, F1 0.1851, recall 0.8713, specificity 0.6611.

## 3. Unfinished

- Native JEPA, ECG-JEPA, and self-supervised PatchTST do not yet have
  completed downstream hypotension test metrics.
- Cross-channel PatchTST, compact PatchTST, and compact InceptionTime have
  only incomplete best-observed validation histories and no completed full-test
  metric artifacts. Canonical InceptionTime has no paired validation metrics
  recorded yet.
- The two-GPU JEPA path has not completed a training step. It fails during
  rank-1 CUDA device setup, even under `torchrun`, on multiple nodes.
- The one-GPU run is only at epoch 0 and has not yet produced validation
  metrics or its first 30-minute rolling checkpoint.
- A full 100-epoch one-GPU run is estimated at roughly 8--9 days, so it must
  span multiple 3-day short-partition allocations.

## 4. Known bugs and caveats

- Two-GPU JEPA rank 1 fails with `CUDA-capable device(s) is/are busy or
  unavailable` on `a100-4029`, `a100-4003`, and the a100_dev debug attempt.
  This is unresolved; do not assume the two-GPU path is usable.
- Test comparisons must remain on the fixed 127,811-window subject split;
  smoke and 10% subset values are not comparable full-test results.
- Validation AUROC and average precision are tracked independently; their best
  values may come from different epochs/checkpoints.
- The one-GPU script is named `*_debug.sbatch` and has a 4-hour dev default.
  Use the command-line partition/time/requeue overrides below for production
  short-partition segments.
- Checkpoint resume requires the same `run_subdir` and a compatible data/model
  fingerprint. A partially written checkpoint may be rejected safely.
- Existing repository caveats include the native JEPA unshared-channel
  `apply_masks` training issue, the misspelled `loss.mape` clamp call,
  attention masks not being passed through `MultiHeadAttention`, and the
  lowercase-only optimizer comparison in `GeneralTimeSupervised`.

## 5. Commands to continue

Activate the prescribed environment:

```bash
source /gpfs/share/apps/anaconda3/gpu/2025.06/etc/profile.d/conda.sh
conda activate physiojepa
cd /gpfs/home/dk5565/PhysioJEPA
```

Check jobs and logs:

```bash
squeue -u dk5565
tail -f /gpfs/data/eh3828lab/derived_datasets/baselines/PhysioJEPA/logs/slurm/physiojepa-jepa-1gpu-short-26107011.out
```

Review the completed metrics and current job state:

```bash
sed -n '1,180p' MODEL_TEST_METRICS.md
sacct -j 26107011 --format=JobID,JobName%28,State,ExitCode,Elapsed,End -n -P
```

Inspect FCN/PatchTST artifacts and reports:

```bash
cat /gpfs/data/eh3828lab/derived_datasets/baselines/PhysioJEPA/models/fcn_hypotension_paper/2026-07-31-fcn-paper-replication-v1/hypotension_label-fcn_baseline_hypotension_paper-paper_metrics.json
sed -n '100,145p' jobs/baselines/SUPERVISED_PATCHTST.md
```
Resubmit the one-GPU segment after walltime or failure. The fixed run
subdirectory allows automatic checkpoint discovery:

```bash
sbatch \
  --partition=a100_short \
  --time=3-00:00:00 \
  --requeue \
  --signal=B:SIGUSR1@180 \
  --job-name=physiojepa-jepa-1gpu-short \
  jobs/jepa/train_patch_jepa_1gpu_debug.sbatch
```

Inspect which checkpoint would be available before restarting:

```bash
find /gpfs/data/eh3828lab/derived_datasets/baselines/PhysioJEPA/models/jepa_native_paper/2026-08-04-native-jepa-paper-1gpu-debug-v1 \
  -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%TY-%Tm-%Td %TH:%TM:%TS|%s|%f\\n' | sort
```

Do not resubmit the two-GPU script until the rank-1 CUDA/device mapping issue
has been diagnosed.
